      "c-cfdde11185f2f07a": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-680",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See also Mark 10:13; Luke 18:15. It was common among the Jews to bring their children to men noted for piety, to have their blessing and their prayers. On the first anniversary of the birth of a child, it was usual to take it to the synagogue to be blessed by the rabbi. The layin…"
      }
